, so discard is less likely to give opponents a pung/kong.  \n- It doesn't help in forming sequences, which our hand needs more of.  \n\nReason: J3 is a \"safe discard\" given its abundance and isolation, and it doesn't hinder future hand development. We need to start consolidating our hand toward sequences or pairs, and discarding honors early is standard strategy when the hand is shapeless.  \n\nAnswer: Play J3"}
